\title{Ford-Fulkerson terminates}
\date{2026-11-12T18:13:55Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\taxon{Lemma}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{The [Ford-Fulkerson algorithm](00SE) terminates (the flow can’t keep getting bigger forever).}

\proof{[Augmenting always increases the flow value](00SG); eventually, if all edges out of #{s} are at capacity, there will be no more forwards edges out of #{s} in #{G_f}, and hence no more paths from #{s} to #{t}.}
